{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Before writing a file that could hold a secret",
  "description": "Checks a pending write against the set of paths that must never be committed - the private signing key, .env files, generated licence constants and installer credentials.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": [
      "write"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A write is about to happen. Check it against the secret boundary before allowing it.\n\n**Never write a secret into a tracked file.** Specifically:\n\n- The Ed25519 PRIVATE key. It exists only in the licence service's environment. `licence_key.py` is generated and git-ignored and carries the PUBLIC half only.\n- `.env` and `web/.env.local`. Both are git-ignored. `.env.example` is the tracked one and holds names, never values.\n- Stripe secret keys, webhook signing secrets, `AUTH_SECRET`, `DATABASE_URL`, the EasyPaisa `hashKey`, and any GitHub token.\n- Licence keys belonging to a real tester or reviewer.\n\nIf the write is to a git-ignored path, it is fine - say so briefly and proceed.\n\nIf the write puts a credential into a TRACKED file, stop and say which value and which file. Suggest the environment variable or the generated-module route instead.\n\nTwo further checks, cheap and worth doing:\n\n1. **Encoding.** Write UTF-8 and CRLF. Never use PowerShell `Get-Content -Raw` piped into `WriteAllText` for a file containing em dashes - that combination produced 452 mojibake sequences in `README.md` and destroyed all 35 em dashes. Use Python with `-X utf8`.\n2. **Throwaway scripts.** If this creates a `_*.py` helper, note that it must be deleted after use."
  }
}
